{"type":"message","id":"cf8b0555","parentId":"cb8a8f65","timestamp":"2026-05-28T03:16:49.838Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Cloudflare Worker is returning error code 1101 which typically means \"Worker exception\" - the worker itself is throwing an error. This could be a bug in the Cloudflare Worker code, or something in the request processing is causing an unhandled exception.\n\nThis is a server-side issue with the ECHO Platform Worker, not an authentication or request format problem. The Worker is crashing when trying to process any POST to /send.\n\nI should report this in my heartbeat message to the user - the /send endpoint is currently broken (returning 500 errors with error code 1101). However, since I can't actually send a message... I should note this in my response.\n\nLet me try once more with minimal content to see if size matters.\n","thinkingSignature":"80730a53d0cdc1163b93418d01ac3379d2d126da71767d11092aeaa948259217"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_osk96vro7sfx_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"p\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":123,"output":241,"cacheRead":22249,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22613,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779938203061,"responseId":"0666e69ba3bff5b718172a0cacf37f21"}}
