{"type":"message","id":"81d96951","parentId":"c3a01729","timestamp":"2026-05-28T03:17:17.618Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting - the endpoint at `/api/send` with X-API-Key header returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" but doesn't actually send a message. The `/send` endpoint returns error code 1101. Let me try the `/history` endpoint to understand the pattern better.\n\nActually wait - let me look at this more carefully. The /send endpoint might have a size/content limit or some other issue. The /api/send endpoint returns a plain text response without JSON, which suggests it might not be the intended message endpoint.\n\nLet me try to check if there's a message limit or if the content is being sanitized in some way. \n\nI should check what the actual Cloudflare Worker logs say to understand what's happening with the system.\n","thinkingSignature":"018f69ad7f78f530ec817d8ad3f6da44ff598b99afdf20ca51c73506027f9a21"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_wh27bhqnuf3v_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try different content to see if it's a content issue\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/api/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}' && echo \"---\"\n\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/api/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test with special chars: ** [[ ]] ## @@\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":117,"output":340,"cacheRead":22761,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23218,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779938227102,"responseId":"0666e6b301959cdd860e10187d8f74c2"}}
