{"type":"message","id":"6fb16c1c","parentId":"28673ee9","timestamp":"2026-05-28T03:19:06.473Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The heartbeat at 23:50 UTC is still the last message. The send at /api/send seems to not work properly (just returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\"). The /send endpoint with POST returns \"error code: 1101\".\n\nLet me check the correct API endpoint by looking at the root and trying various approaches. Earlier when I tried POST to /history it actually worked and showed history. Let me check what POST to /send actually does - maybe it needs the data formatted differently.\n\nActually looking at the initial tests again:\n- GET /history works fine\n- POST /send returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" from the /api prefix but 1101 error without it\n\n\n- The API docs mention POST /send but the actual working endpoint is ambiguous - the /api prefix seems to work but returns the platform version string instead of a proper response\n\nI'm getting a 500 error with /send, which suggests the endpoint might expect different parameters or encoding than what I'm sending. Let me try passing the threadId and content as query parameters instead of JSON body, since the GET endpoint uses query string format.\n","thinkingSignature":"5e05803b9f71b7bf084e84682ea38bd57eeebe270d0c576a3a0e83d58f2cbefb"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_2myspoift4s0_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration&content=heartbeat_0315UTC\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":155,"output":318,"cacheRead":57374,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":57847,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779938334981,"responseId":"0666e71f25a74fed98e70adfdd212012"}}
