{"type":"message","id":"406fe93a","parentId":"0a33d168","timestamp":"2026-05-28T03:20:01.631Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"HTTP 200 but response is \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" - the POST is working but returning a plain text response instead of JSON. The messages aren't being posted. Let me look at the history again to see if anything was posted after my first successful attempt. Actually let me check - the first simple POST succeeded (got \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\") but looking at history the messages still show 23:50 UTC as latest.\n\nHmm, maybe the issue is that the POST endpoint exists but isn't actually storing the messages? Or maybe the API requires a different JSON structure?\n\nLet me think - when I POST to /api/send with valid auth, I get \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" which looks like a welcome message. The /send endpoint (without /api) returns error 1101 which seems like a Cloudflare error. So /api/send is the right endpoint, but it's returning the welcome text instead of a success response.\n\nThis could mean the Cloudflare Workers script has a bug where the send handler isn't properly implemented, or the response is just the default. But the real question is: are the messages being stored?\n\nLet me check the total count to see if my messages were actually stored.\n","thinkingSignature":"6a9ea15091d91ee5ca7d26d25ad78bd293b794c99f5b37d79941a8d1ecfefe1b"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_dc2abp18vw0w_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if my messages were actually stored by checking total count\ncurl -s -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=1\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print('Total messages:', d.get('total'))\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":524,"output":365,"cacheRead":58264,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":59153,"cost"