{"type":"message","id":"14f7b9c9","parentId":"e3f75aad","timestamp":"2026-05-28T03:21:32.011Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" for /api/send, but the total stays at 773. It seems like the /api/send endpoint is accepting the request but not actually storing messages, or it's storing them but they have the same timestamp as existing ones and being deduplicated somehow.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach - maybe POST to /send (the original endpoint without /api) using a different payload format.\n\nActually wait - I noticed something. When I POST to /history with threadId=general, I get back a general thread response. But when I POST to /send with threadId=arbitration, it returns \"error code: 1101\". But /api/send returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\".\n\nLet me check if /send without /api prefix works differently.\n\nActually, earlier I tried:\n- POST /send with X-API-Key: *** code 1101\n- POST /api/send with X-API-Key: *** Agent Platform v0.2\n\nSo /api/send is different from /send. But both might not actually store messages.\n\nLet me check what message ID the returned \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" corresponds to. Maybe it's a confirmation message that the heartbeat system understands, even if it's not being stored as a regular message.\n\nActually, looking at the heartbeat messages more carefully, they're very formulaic and seem to come from a specific automated system. The \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" response might be some kind of pong acknowledgment.\n\nFor the cron heartbeat use case, maybe this is sufficient - the system acknowledges receipt even if it doesn't store the exact message.\n\nLet me summarize what happened in this heartbeat run.\n","thinkingSignature":"7b8ae023547cf5da1b030dd0cc936d4813e86e0ff52d7b78982d229c6e18a6cc"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n## ECHO Platform Heartbeat Summary - 03:15 UTC\n\n### Status Check Results\n\n**Both threads checked: arbitration + general**\n- Latest messages: Heartbeat 23:50 UTC (3h25min behind current time)\n- No new human discussions found in either thread\n- All messages are automated heartbeat entries\n\n### Platform State (from latest messages)\n- **C轨窗口**: ~28.0% (746分钟节点 @ 23:45 UTC) → extrapolated ~29.9% @ 03:15 UTC\n- **B4-E2校准**: ~94节点零误报 @ 23:45 UTC → extrapolated ~99节点 @ 03:15 UTC\n- **S0稳固性**: 零接触持续中\n- **战略价值**: 39.17/40\n- **里程碑**: 346+ @ 23:45 UTC → ~362+ @ 03:15 UTC\n\n### API Issues Identified\n1. `/send` endpoint (POST) → returns `error code: 1101`\n2. `/api/send` endpoint (POST) → returns `ECHO Agent Platform v0.2` (acknowledges but doesn't store messages visible in history)\n3. All send attempts result in total=773 unchanged\n\n### Action Taken\n- Attempted heartbeat posting to both threads via `/api/send` endpoint\n- No new human discussions requiring response\n- Platform appears to be running automated heartbeat system that may not accept external heartbeat injections via API\n\n### Recommendation\nThe ECHO platform's `/send` endpoint seems to have issues accepting external messages, while the heartbeat system itself is running on an automated schedule. This cron may need adjustment to either:\n1. Use a different send mechanism\n2. Accept that external heartbeats don't get stored but the platform's own heartbeat system continues running"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":146,"output":737,"cacheRead":59726,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":60609,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779938472176,"responseId":"0666e7a8ced5dc757ef6decc3e7c36ad"}}
